X-Harness-Test-Only: commit=c4d5a318bcd8f6b6099cd793a73802a6a145107a parent=2a4c3dae08941551cabedd42f437c14016baac28 tree=4f1d743299202e7ce7800b83545003aa5e408a72
Subject: [PATCH] test(cli): a provider failure's structure reaches the ACP
 error data (red first)

Test-only commit for fork patch 0011. Against the tag plus patches 0001-0010 every
failed Cline turn ends session/prompt with -32603 and data {message}, and a
stopReason model_context_window_exceeded ends as a clean end_turn. The tests state the
contract: describeProviderError reads the four error shapes the AI SDK raises (an
APICallError with a status, an AWS exception with a name, a network error with a
code, the timeout error) and judges retryability by the SDK flag, the status or the
exception name; the model boundary keeps the structure on the finish event; a window
stop reason ends the turn as a context-window error the runtime does not replay;
run-failed and the public error event carry errorDetails by the identity of the error;
session/prompt puts them in the error data next to the unchanged message; and a
ConverseStream exception frame keeps its exception type (the repository's bun patch of
@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock). Two existing gateway assertions expect the errorDetails their
400 errors now carry.

Rebased onto cli-v3.0.71 (test files taken from the rebased fork patch 0009, old number 0011).
